::2025_CS2_Q44:: Consider a system of linear equations 𝑃𝑋 \= 𝑄 where 𝑃 ∈ ℝ3×3 and Q ∈ ℝ3×1 . Suppose 𝑃 has an LU decomposition, 𝑃 \= 𝐿𝑈, where 𝑙 𝐿 \= [ 21 𝑙31 𝑙32 𝑢11 0] and 𝑈 \= [ 0 𝑢12 𝑢22 𝑢13 𝑢23 ]. 𝑢33 Which of the following statement(s) is/are TRUE? {
    =The system 𝑃𝑋 \= 𝑄 can be solved by first solving 𝐿𝑌 \= 𝑄 and then 𝑈𝑋 \= 𝑌.
    ~If 𝑃 is invertible, then both 𝐿 and 𝑈 are invertible.
    ~If 𝑃 is singular, then at least one of the diagonal elements of 𝑈 is zero.
    ~If 𝑃 is symmetric, then both 𝐿 and 𝑈 are symmetric.
}

